 # Sparsity Regularization
 ## Overview
-Sparsity regularization is a technique used in radiance-field optimization to encourage model emptiness, thereby reducing unstructured artifacts and preventing the prediction of background color in empty space [S1, S2]. It sets itself apart from homogeneity-based methods like Total Variation by specifically penalizing non-zero density values to favor a sparse voxel grid [S2]. It builds on [Plenoxels regularization ablation](901-plenoxels-regularization-ablation.md) and complements siblings such as [Sparsity and Beta Loss Regularization](1392-sparsity-and-beta-loss-regularization.md) and [Plenoxel Optimization with TV Regularization](1132-plenoxel-optimization-with-tv-regularization.md).
